+++ b/docs/PS2RECOMP_PATCHES.md
@@ -389,3 +389,9 @@ changes keep desktop behaviour: `main()` and `run()` take the same steps as befo
 | Where | What | Why |
 |---|---|---|
 | `ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_audio_out.cpp`, `include/runtime/ps2_audio_out.h`; `src/game/vcs_sound.cpp` | `ps2AudioSetFiller`: a keeper thread (started in `ps2AudioInit`, joined in `ps2AudioShutdown`) asks the producer for more when the ring holds under 40 ms and nothing was pushed for 15 ms; the native sound driver's filler mixes the SPU2 ahead of EE time under its lock, and `clock()` mixes only past it. While not primed (at start, after an underrun) the keeper fills up to the target, in whole 256-frame blocks (the SPU2's hand-over size), so it cannot stop just short of priming; it is idle while a movie's sound is queued (the SPU2 is not mixed under a movie, as before). The runtime forgives an IOP lag over 1 s (PS2Runtime::advanceIopEeCycles), so a stall's time beyond 1 s never reaches `clock()`; a filler lead over 1 s therefore moves the engine's EE time along, the EE repays the rest and `clock()` mixes again (without it the filler mixed everything after a 2 s stall). `runEnd` calls `ps2AudioShutdown` before `platform::shutdown` (the header's order): the keeper is joined before the device closes. The stats line gives the filled share. On by default on the Switch only (`__SWITCH__`); `PS2X_AUDIO_FILL=1` / `0` overrides; off with `PS2X_IOP_REALTIME=0` | The SPU2 was mixed only on the game thread: a frame longer than the target fill (60-250 ms) was a gap, and the catch-up burst after it overflowed the 400 ms cap and was dropped. On the Switch (frames of 0.5-1 s while driving) a 16-minute drive starved 54 s in 169 underruns |
+
+## The Switch port's developer menu (Switch port M08, 2026-11-19)
+
+| Where | What | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_perf.cpp`, `include/runtime/ps2_perf.h` | `ps2perf::setRecording` / `recording` / `recordingName`: F4's CSV recording started and stopped from a menu, into a given folder | The Switch has no F4: its developer menu (L3 + R3) starts and stops the frame-time recording, and writes it under the game folder's userdata instead of the working directory (the extracted disc) |
